---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ScrollReveal from "../../components/ScrollReveal.astro";

const highlights = [
  "Taekwondo Instructor @ Koo's Martial Arts 2017-2021",
  "Warehouse Worker @ Amazon Warehouse 2021",
  "Tutor @ UC Santa Cruz 2021-2023",
  "Peer Navigator @ UC Santa Cruz 2021-2022",
  "Software Engineer @ Roblox 2025-present",
  "Software Engineer Intern @ Maxar Technologies 2022",
  "Software Engineer Intern @ Roblox 2024",
  "Research Assistant @ SCIPP 2022",
];
---

<Layout title="About" activeId="about">
  <div class="page-content">
    <header class="gear-hero">
      <h1 class="gear-title">Hello :)</h1>
      <p class="gear-subheader">I'm William (but you can call me Will)</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="gear-hero-image">
      <img src="/KamakuraJapan.jpg" alt="Kamakura, Japan in February 2026" />
      <figcaption>
        At <a
          href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kōtoku-in"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Kōtoku-in</a
        > in <a
          href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamakura"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Kamakura, Japan</a
        > during February 2026
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="page-card-section">
      <p class="page-card-text">
        I'm a Software Engineer focused on scalable, reliable infrastructure. My
        work centers on request and runtime configuration systems. I enjoy
        making behavior explicit, observable, and safe to change. A few years in
        industry has led me to two truths:
      </p>
      <ul class="page-card-text">
        <li>There are multiple solutions to any problem.</li>
        <li>
          Experience, communication, and product understanding are needed for
          great work.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="page-card-text">
        My philosophy is that the <span class="italic">perfect solution</span> includes
        pragmatism and iteration. I would rather ship, improve, and adapt a good solution
        than wait for perfect.
      </p>
      <p class="page-card-text">
        In retrospect, my attitude shift was gradual. I used to dislike
        programming. It was (still is) difficult and time-consuming. Though, one
        day during university, I thought 'Huh, this is actually fun.' I then
        wrapped up my undergrad at <a
          href="https://www.ucsc.edu/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">UCSC</a
        >, then my Masters in Computer Science at <a
          href="https://www.ucla.edu/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">UCLA</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p class="page-card-text">
        Outside work, I play video games, boulder, and tinker with projects
        (link to my <a
          href="https://fumoarchive.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">latest project</a
        >). I also enjoy learning new things. I'm currently focused on:
        <ul class="page-card-text">
          <li>Studying Japanese</li>
          <li>Expanding my wardrobe</li>
          <li>Being healthy</li>
        </ul>
      </p>
      <h2 class="gear-section-title">Work</h2>
      <p class="page-card-text">
        I work on the Configurations Team at <a
          href="https://careers.roblox.com/work-at-roblox"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Roblox</a
        >. We manage multiple critical services (8M+ requests per second) with
        high availability and reliability. Name any Roblox service and we
        probably serve its configuratiohn.
      </p>
      <figure class="gear-hero-image">
        <img src="/BlockyGame.png" alt="Playing Roblox with my twin brother" />
        <figcaption>Playing Roblox with my twin brother</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="page-card-text">
        Before Roblox, I interned at <a
          href="https://www.maxar.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Maxar Technologies</a
        >, building satellite software, including the
        <a
          href="https://www.intelsat.com/launches/galaxy-31-and-galaxy-32/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Galaxy-31 and Galaxy-32 Intelsat C-band Satellites</a
        > launched by SpaceX. I also did research at the <a
          href="https://scipp.ucsc.edu/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Santa Cruz Institute for Particle Physics</a
        >, building an ML program to identify Higgs boson particles. Aside from
        my aforementioned work, I worked several part-time jobs to support
        myself through college, including warehouse, tutoring, taekwondo
        instructor, and peer navigator roles.
      </p>
    </section>
    <ScrollReveal items={highlights} />
    <h2 class="gear-section-title">Social Links</h2>
    <ul class="page-card-text">
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/williamsantosa/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/williamsantosa"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="mailto:williamwsantosa@gmail.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Email</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
